### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 4: media
### VS Code REST Client. Run the requests top-to-bottom; the @variables carry state forward.
### Session cookies are handled by the REST Client automatically; CSRF is echoed by hand.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Sign in to the admin realm (sets cw_adm_at / cw_adm_rt / cw_adm_csrf)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@clearwood.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe@12345"
}

###
@csrf = {{adminLogin.response.headers.$['set-cookie'][2]}}

### 2. What will the server accept? (limits, rendition ladder, active driver)
GET {{api}}/admin/media/config

### 3. Upload a file.
### REST Client builds the multipart body from the boundary below — point the path at any
### local image. `files` is the field name; repeat the part to upload several at once.
# @name upload
POST {{api}}/admin/media/upload
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ClearWoodBoundary

--ClearWoodBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="folderPath"

products
--ClearWoodBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--ClearWoodBoundary--

###
@mediaId = {{upload.response.body.data.uploaded[0].media.id}}

### 4. Re-uploading the same bytes returns the existing asset with deduplicated: true.

### 5. Browse the library (R5 pagination meta, filters, search)
GET {{api}}/admin/media?page=1&limit=20&status=READY&sort=createdAt&order=desc

### 6. Search by name, alt text or tag
GET {{api}}/admin/media?q=teak

### 7. Full detail, including every rendition and every usage
GET {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}

### 8. Edit the metadata an editor cares about
PATCH {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "altText": "Teak sideboard in a sunlit living room",
  "title": "Teak sideboard",
  "tags": ["teak", "storage"],
  "focalPoint": { "x": 45, "y": 35 }
}

### 9. Invalid focal point → 422 with field details (R2)
PATCH {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "focalPoint": { "x": 400, "y": -5 } }

### 10. The media folder tree (system folders cannot be renamed or deleted)
GET {{api}}/admin/media-folders

### 11. Pick a product to attach the asset to
# @name products
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories?limit=1

### Replace this with a real product id from your seed (see /api/v1/catalog/categories/{slug}).
@productId = REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID

### 12. Attach it to a product gallery
POST {{api}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/media
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "items": [
    { "mediaId": "{{mediaId}}", "role": "GALLERY", "deviceTarget": "ALL" }
  ]
}

### 13. The current gallery links for that product
GET {{api}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/media

### 14. Reorder the gallery (positions are rewritten in the order given)
PATCH {{api}}/admin/products/{{productId}}/media/reorder
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "items": [
    { "id": "REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_MEDIA_ID", "position": 0 }
  ]
}

### 15. The public gallery — no auth, resolved ordering, variant/colour/device aware
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/teak-sideboard/gallery

### 16. Narrowed to one variant
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/teak-sideboard/gallery?variantId=REPLACE_WITH_VARIANT_ID&device=MOBILE

### 17. Hard delete is refused while the asset is referenced → 409 MEDIA_IN_USE
DELETE {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}/permanent
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 18. …and succeeds with ?force=true, which detaches every usage first (audited as CRITICAL)
DELETE {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}/permanent?force=true
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 19. Soft delete / restore (D6 — the row and the files survive)
DELETE {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}/restore
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 20. Regenerate renditions after changing the preset table
POST {{api}}/admin/media/{{mediaId}}/reprocess
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 21. Bulk move to trash
POST {{api}}/admin/media/bulk-delete
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "ids": ["{{mediaId}}"] }

### 22. Orphan report — dry run only, never deletes
GET {{api}}/admin/media/gc

### 23. Presigned upload: 501 on the local driver, a real ticket on S3
POST {{api}}/admin/media/presign
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "fileName": "hero.jpg", "contentType": "image/jpeg", "sizeBytes": 812345 }
